Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:02.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Those gaps are where this film lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.45,0:00:06.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The study behind this\Nfilm asks three things.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.15,0:00:10.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One: can a {\c&HF09CB4&}machine{\c&HF7F4F2&} learn\Nthe whole family of fields,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.70,0:00:13.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}even at knob settings between the dots?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.42,0:00:17.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Two: can it respect\Neach law where it holds,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.82,0:00:22.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}exactly in every field,\Nor {\c&H00A1ED&}on average{\c&HF7F4F2&} over many fields?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.02,0:00:26.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Three: can it tell us\N{\c&H00A1ED&}how often{\c&HF7F4F2&} the field flips?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.57,0:00:30.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}To find out, the study's\Nplan climbs a staircase,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.79,0:00:34.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}from three numbers to the\Nshapes of real experiments.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.35,0:00:39.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One honest note: this\Nindependent study is prospective,
